  "answer": "Based on the current data from the **U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA)** Gasoline and Diesel Fuel Update (as of September 21, 2026), the average US on-highway diesel price is **$6.529 per gallon**.\n\nUsing a fuel efficiency of **6.5 mpg**, the fuel costs for the specified trip legs are as follows:\n\n### Fuel Cost Summary\n\n| Leg | Distance (miles) | Gallons (Distance / 6.5) | Cost (Gallons × $6.529) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Chicago–Indianapolis | 185 | 28.46 | $185.82 |\n| Indianapolis–Columbus | 175 | 26.92 | $175.78 |\n| Columbus–Pittsburgh | 185 | 28.46 | $185.82 |\n| **Total** | **545** | **83.85** | **$547.43** |\n\n*Note: The total cost is calculated from raw values to avoid rounding drift; summing the rounded leg costs would result in $547.42, whereas the precise total is $547.43.*\n\n### Excel File Details (`fuel_costs.xlsx`)\nThe professional Excel workbook has been constructed to ensure mathematical precision and ease of updates:\n\n*   **Dynamic Inputs & Named Ranges:**\n    *   **Diesel Price** ($6.529) is located in cell `B1` and defined as the named range `Diesel_Price`.\n    *   **Fuel Efficiency** (6.5 mpg) is located in cell `B2` and defined as the named range `Fuel_Efficiency`.\n    *   Both input cells are highlighted with a **light yellow fill** for clear identification.\n*   **Formula-Driven Table:**\n    *   **Gallons Column:** Uses the formula `=[Distance]/Fuel_Efficiency` (e.g., `=B5/Fuel_Efficiency`).\n    *   **Cost Column:** Uses the formula `=[Gallons]*Diesel_Price` (e.g., `=C5*Diesel_Price`).\n    *   **Total Row:** Uses `=SUM()` formulas for Distance, Gallons, and Cost. By summing the raw formula results rather than the displayed rounded values, the file maintains absolute precision.\n*   **Professional Formatting:**\n    *   **Font:** Arial throughout the entire workbook.\n    *   **Currency:** All cost cells are formatted as currency (`$#,##0.00`).\n    *   **Layout:** The data table includes professional borders, centered headers, and optimized column widths.\n*   **Citation:** A source note is included in cell `A11`: *\"Source: U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA), Gasoline and Diesel Fuel Update, 09/21/26, https://www.eia.gov/petroleum/gasdiesel/\"*",
